{#
mail/account.html.twig — one account's INBOX.

Reached by clicking the account itself in the sidebar. It used to be every
thread in the account whatever it was labelled, which meant your own sent mail
interleaved through what had arrived, with drafts and spam among it — an
archive, where a person clicking their address means "show me what came in".
Everything else in the account is a folder row one click below it.

The heading names the account AND says Inbox, because those two facts together
are the only thing that distinguishes this screen from the unified inbox above
it and from the account's other folders beside it.
#}
{% extends '_layout/_mailbox.html.twig' %}

{% block title %}{{ account.displayAddress }} — {{ 'app.name'|trans }}{% endblock %}

{% block inbox_tabs %}
    {% import '_partials/_category_tab_glyphs.html.twig' as glyphs %}

    <div class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-line flex items-center gap-2">
        <h2 class="text-sm font-semibold text-ink-soft">{{ 'sidebar.nav.inbox'|trans }}</h2>
        <span class="text-xs text-ink-faint truncate">{{ account.displayAddress }}</span>
    </div>

    {# The category tabs, for this account's mail.

       The same five as the unified inbox and chosen by the same rule — one
       exists while it holds mail, the one you are on stays — but deliberately
       plainer: an icon and a name. What the unified strip adds is a set of
       counters ("3 new", the sender hint, the unread tint) that are summed
       across EVERY account and rewritten by the sidebar controller from that
       same payload. Drawn here they would describe the wrong mailbox, and be
       overwritten with the wrong numbers after the next sync, so they are not
       drawn; the keys they are patched by are not emitted either. Dragging a
       conversation onto a tab is the unified inbox's, for the same reason: its
       targets are built from that page's counts.

       Links go to THIS page with `?tab=`, carrying whatever else narrows the
       list and dropping `page`, because page four of Primary is not page four
       of Social. The strip scrolls inside itself rather than squeezing, since
       five tabs are wider than a phone. #}
    {% set tabQuery = app.request.query.all|filter((v, k) => k not in ['tab', 'page']) %}

    {% if tabs|length > 1 %}
        <div class="border-b border-line px-1">
            <nav class="flex text-sm overflow-x-auto overflow-y-hidden pb-px -mb-px [scrollbar-width:none] [&::-webkit-scrollbar]:hidden">
                {% for tabCase in tabs %}
                    {% set isActive = tabCase === tab %}
                    <a
                        href="{{ path('app_mail_account', {account: account.id}|merge(tabQuery)|merge({tab: tabCase.value})) }}"
                        data-turbo-frame="inbox-list-frame"
                        {% if isActive %}aria-current="page"{% endif %}
                        class="flex items-center gap-2.5 px-3 @xl:px-5 py-1.5 min-h-14 font-medium border-b-2 -mb-px transition-colors shrink-0 whitespace-nowrap {{ isActive ? 'text-accent border-accent' : 'text-ink-muted hover:text-gray-700 border-transparent hover:border-gray-300' }}"
                    >
                        {% if isActive %}
                            <svg class="w-5 h-5 shrink-0" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="currentColor" aria-hidden="true">
                                <path fill-rule="evenodd" clip-rule="evenodd" d="{{ glyphs.solid(tabCase.value) }}"/>
                            </svg>
                        {% else %}
                            <svg class="w-5 h-5 shrink-0" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" aria-hidden="true">
                                <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="{{ glyphs.outline(tabCase.value) }}"/>
                            </svg>
                        {% endif %}
                        {{ ('tabs.' ~ tabCase.value)|trans }}
                    </a>
                {% endfor %}
            </nav>
        </div>
    {% endif %}
{% endblock %}

{% block message_list %}
    {% if threads is empty %}
        <li class="px-4 py-8 text-center text-sm text-ink-faint">
            {{ 'inbox.empty_account'|trans }}
        </li>
    {% else %}
        {% for thread in threads %}
            {# Every row here is the same account, so the dot would say nothing. #}
            {% include '_partials/_thread_row.html.twig' with { thread: thread, unified: false } %}
        {% endfor %}
    {% endif %}
{% endblock %}
